      "name": "e2e_dom",
      "description": "Summarise the rendered DOM so blank-screen and whether a required element exists can be judged without a screenshot. Each node carries a stable CSS selector, tag, text and rect (in logical CSS px, same space as e2e_screenshot and e2e_interact x/y). For canvas / game artifacts this also returns sceneTree — the read-only Pixi/Three scene hierarchy from the simulator inspector. Each scene node has: ref (unique, `<providerId>:<node>`), label, visible, selectable (whether it can be hit), and source.file + source.definitionKey (source location). Multiple canvases appear as multiple providers (each with providerId + engine); refs are providerId-prefixed so they stay unique.",
